WEBVTT

00:14.670 --> 00:29.140
hitotsume no kotoba wa yume nemuri no naka kara

00:14.670 --> 00:29.140
The first word was "dream", it came to me as I slept.

00:31.230 --> 00:44.810
mune no oku no kurayami wo sotto tsuredasu no

00:31.230 --> 00:44.810
Gently bringing out the darkness deep inside my heart.

00:47.910 --> 01:02.850
futatsume no kotoba wa kaze yukute wo oshiete

00:47.910 --> 01:02.850
The second word was "wind", show me the way...

01:04.220 --> 01:18.180
kamisama no ude no naka e tsubasa wo aoru no

01:04.220 --> 01:18.180
I beat my wings towards the embrace of the gods.

01:19.820 --> 01:34.210
tokete itta kanashii koto wo kazoeru you ni

01:19.820 --> 01:34.210
As if counting the sorrows that have melted all away...

01:35.630 --> 01:44.220
kin'iro no ringo ga

01:35.630 --> 01:44.220
The golden apples fall...

01:45.550 --> 01:52.230
mata hitotsu ochiru

01:45.550 --> 01:52.230
Falling one at a time...

02:05.350 --> 02:08.480
1-0-7! That was my target!

02:09.730 --> 02:12.610
Come on, come on, come on! Yes!

02:12.610 --> 02:13.520
Wha...?!

02:14.730 --> 02:16.150
What the hell's your problem?!

02:17.950 --> 02:19.530
Are you trying to kill me?!

02:21.780 --> 02:24.660
You take too long with these small fries and they'll get behind you.

02:24.660 --> 02:27.500
Shit! My gun pod's jammed!
Mayday! Mayday!

02:30.670 --> 02:32.170
1-0-3, don't move!

02:42.050 --> 02:44.260
These punks aren't any sorta challenge at all.

02:51.940 --> 02:53.270
Maybe I spoke too soon!

02:57.900 --> 02:59.190
I hate being disappointed, pal.

03:08.950 --> 03:12.080
Can't I find some decent guys to fight?!

03:20.340 --> 03:21.300
Transferred?!

03:21.800 --> 03:24.600
That's right.
You understand why, don't you?

03:24.600 --> 03:25.510
No, I don't!

03:26.260 --> 03:28.100
Seven instances of disobeying orders.

03:28.100 --> 03:32.560
Five times under house arrest,
flight command revoked six times.

03:33.600 --> 03:37.440
You should be grateful we
haven't court-martialed you.

03:37.440 --> 03:38.780
Where are you sending me?

03:39.780 --> 03:42.700
Perhaps to maintenance patrol for the Echo satellites.

03:42.700 --> 03:45.780
Or to planetary fragment disposal at Barnard's Star.

03:45.780 --> 03:49.200
Or perhaps to the coal mines
of planet Banipal, or maybe...

03:50.410 --> 03:55.880
But none of them want a nutty hotshot like you.

03:56.880 --> 03:59.510
So we've decided to send you here.

04:01.130 --> 04:06.050
Planet Eden...
New Edwards Test Flight Center...

04:07.300 --> 04:10.850
Now listen, the only enemy
a test pilot has to deal with...

04:11.270 --> 04:14.730
...is himself! You've got to try and consider...

04:15.190 --> 04:18.150
You're making me a test pilot, aren't you?!

04:18.150 --> 04:20.190
Dammit! Isamu, listen to
your commander for once!

04:20.690 --> 04:23.320
Lt. Dyson, gladly leaving for new assignment, sir!

04:57.060 --> 05:00.320
Number two and three optical and electronic systems: check.

05:02.150 --> 05:05.030
Brainwave Control System connection: nominal.

05:11.990 --> 05:14.710
Brain waves: Beta wave is flat.

05:14.710 --> 05:17.620
Theta wave needs 1.3 to be connected to the sensor.

05:17.620 --> 05:19.170
Biofeedback: nominal.

05:20.460 --> 05:23.460
Man-Machine wave contacted. Synchronization complete.

05:23.460 --> 05:27.340
Chief Guld, initiate connection to Brain Direct Imaging System.

05:27.840 --> 05:28.800
Roger.

05:46.360 --> 05:48.110
BDI system: nominal.

05:49.030 --> 05:52.080
YF-21 Omega One, standby to launch.

06:57.390 --> 06:58.350
Th-The hell...?!

07:02.980 --> 07:07.860
This is Eagle 1-0-7 to New Edwards. Do you read me?

07:07.860 --> 07:09.360
New Edwards here. Go ahead.

07:10.200 --> 07:15.030
Just had a bogey fly by in
area seven, altitude 38,000.

07:15.030 --> 07:18.040
My radar can't see it. Can you confirm?

07:18.040 --> 07:21.460
Area seven...
Don't worry about that.

07:21.460 --> 07:23.330
Can't explain at present.

07:24.040 --> 07:27.420
W-Wait... Was that the new
fighter they're talking about?

07:29.420 --> 07:30.550
Cool!

07:45.860 --> 07:48.820
Hello Edwards... This is
Lieutenant Isamu Dyson...

07:57.160 --> 07:57.740
Hello there.

07:58.660 --> 08:01.330
I am the eagerly awaited Lt. Isamu Dyson.

08:01.330 --> 08:02.790
Reporting for duty.

08:07.040 --> 08:09.590
So, when do I fly?

08:11.550 --> 08:13.970
I think you should take a little break.

08:13.970 --> 08:15.590
I'm Millard, Chief Planner for the project.

08:16.050 --> 08:18.260
I heard you're a real hothead.

08:18.260 --> 08:18.930
Yes, sir.

08:18.930 --> 08:20.930
You don't like promotions?

08:20.930 --> 08:24.560
No, sir. Too many promotions and they don't let you fly.

08:25.310 --> 08:31.030
I see... Well, I hope you'll be
more ambitious with this project.

08:34.530 --> 08:35.780
Have a seat.

08:35.780 --> 08:36.410
Sir.

08:39.660 --> 08:42.660
The Super Nova Project is testing and developing...

08:42.660 --> 08:47.420
...the candidates for the next
main variable fighter to replace...

08:47.420 --> 08:50.380
...our current VF-11 Thunderbolt.

08:51.340 --> 08:55.800
So as to deal with colony planet disputes or alien threats...

08:55.800 --> 08:59.100
...it will be able to perform
a Hyperspace Fold on its own...

08:59.100 --> 09:02.350
...to advance to close range to its target.

09:05.060 --> 09:09.400
Without the political risks
of using Reflex weaponry...

09:09.400 --> 09:13.070
...the new fighter can break
through the enemy's defenses...

09:13.070 --> 09:15.860
...and destroy only their
center, or rescue hostages.

09:16.280 --> 09:23.620
Shinsei Industries' YF-19 and General Galaxy's YF-21 are the two planes we're currently testing.

09:23.620 --> 09:26.830
The better one will win the project.

09:31.340 --> 09:33.510
So, when can I fly?

09:33.510 --> 09:36.180
How's the schedule look for the YF-19?

09:36.180 --> 09:36.760
Yes, sir.

09:37.890 --> 09:41.310
It'll be back from the factory within a week.

09:41.310 --> 09:42.430
A week?

09:43.180 --> 09:46.060
It's being repaired because of a test flight accident.

09:46.060 --> 09:48.480
You guys've had some bad luck with your pilots.

09:48.980 --> 09:53.190
Well, now that I'm here
everything's okay, no problem.

09:53.190 --> 09:57.860
All the other pilots said the same thing...

09:57.860 --> 09:59.780
...until they actually flew the plane.

10:00.280 --> 10:03.790
Four of them are giving the health plan a whirl.

10:03.790 --> 10:07.210
Two of them received a double promotion... in their coffins.

10:07.210 --> 10:08.370
Who the hell are you?

10:09.210 --> 10:11.960
Kids shouldn't butt into
grown-ups' conversations.

10:11.960 --> 10:14.970
Why don't you just take a
shit and go beddy-bye, okay?

10:15.150 --> 10:20.510
A pilot should be able to
grasp his situation instantly.

10:20.510 --> 10:23.930
Why would an ordinary kid be attending this meeting?

10:27.810 --> 10:30.520
Umm... Is he your son, Chief?

10:33.070 --> 10:37.570
This is Yang Neumann, design chief of YF-19 you'll be flying.

10:38.150 --> 10:39.240
Him?

10:39.240 --> 10:44.160
Age, sex, and race are
meaningless concepts here.

10:44.160 --> 10:45.580
Well excuse me!

10:45.580 --> 10:46.540
May I come in?

10:53.540 --> 10:57.300
Let me introduce you. This is
the test pilot for General Galaxy.

10:57.300 --> 10:59.170
Chief Guld Goa Bowman.

11:00.050 --> 11:02.890
He's a test pilot now...?

11:02.890 --> 11:08.430
Their brainwave controlled
YF-21 fighter is epoch-making.

11:08.430 --> 11:09.140
Chief Bowman...

11:09.520 --> 11:14.190
...this is Lt. Isamu Dyson,
pilot for the YF-19 team.

11:15.690 --> 11:18.070
Colonel, about today's flight.

11:18.820 --> 11:21.610
Calibration of the Thought
Control System is going well.

11:21.610 --> 11:24.950
We can start the fire control tests within three days.

11:24.950 --> 11:27.540
That must've been you I saw in area seven!

11:28.000 --> 11:31.000
Sounds like good news, Chief.

11:31.000 --> 11:32.620
I suppose you just can't wait.

11:33.000 --> 11:35.130
I'm afraid he'll just be a waste of time, sir.

11:35.130 --> 11:36.090
Say what?!

11:36.590 --> 11:39.670
You'll just be losing a high-priced fighter...

11:39.670 --> 11:42.680
...to a pilot with no self-control.

11:44.060 --> 11:45.890
Who the hell are you talking about?!

11:46.930 --> 11:48.970
Thanks for just proving my point.

11:52.810 --> 11:54.980
If you want out, now's the time.

11:54.980 --> 11:57.440
I wouldn't bother unpacking if I were you.

11:58.820 --> 12:01.240
Looks like they know each other.

12:01.240 --> 12:03.490
They seem to get along quite well.

12:03.490 --> 12:04.240
Excuse me?

12:48.830 --> 12:52.160
Anti-Laser Coating, Pinpoint Barrier System...

12:52.910 --> 12:55.540
And the new Active
Aerodynamic Control System...

13:24.150 --> 13:26.210
Looks like I died.

13:26.210 --> 13:29.780
Try and take this a little
seriously! One more time!

13:30.200 --> 13:33.000
Dead men can't come back to life.

13:33.410 --> 13:35.290
Let's call it a day. Bye-bye.

13:36.670 --> 13:38.750
Hold it...

13:38.750 --> 13:39.670
Hold it!

13:40.500 --> 13:44.130
At this rate we'll never
catch up to General Galaxy!

13:44.130 --> 13:45.260
Are you listening?!

13:48.800 --> 13:52.310
Lay off of me, or I'll eat you.

13:53.560 --> 13:56.890
Hey, babe! Wanna go out for a drink to mourn my death?

14:05.360 --> 14:08.030
Hey! Slow down! This is dangerous!

14:18.750 --> 14:23.090
Stop it! I don't wanna commit double suicide with you!!!

14:23.750 --> 14:25.170
Thrilling, right?!

14:33.560 --> 14:35.310
You're truly weird.

14:35.310 --> 14:35.850
Me?

14:36.810 --> 14:39.480
I heard there used to be a forest around here.

14:40.270 --> 14:41.940
And some people who climbed that mountain back then...

14:41.940 --> 14:43.860
...saw a giant pterosaur?

14:43.860 --> 14:45.190
You know about that?

14:45.650 --> 14:49.570
They used to call me the roughneck of Dalmatian High School!

14:49.570 --> 14:52.490
You jerk! Why didn't you say so before?

14:56.790 --> 15:00.460
That singing... No, it couldn't be...

15:00.460 --> 15:01.830
It's Sharon.

15:02.290 --> 15:05.170
She'll be here soon. It's gonna be great.

15:05.170 --> 15:08.300
She sounds like an old friend of mine.

15:09.380 --> 15:10.930
You wish.

15:10.930 --> 15:11.890
Huh?

15:11.890 --> 15:13.970
Sharon isn't human.

15:13.970 --> 15:15.350
Not human...?

15:16.850 --> 15:17.890
Oh well!

15:24.730 --> 15:26.320
Un peu de bleu

15:24.730 --> 15:26.320
A little of blue

15:26.320 --> 15:29.990
Pour noir de la matière

15:26.320 --> 15:29.990
For the black of the matter

15:35.120 --> 15:36.700
Un peu de bleu

15:35.120 --> 15:36.700
A little of blue

15:36.700 --> 15:39.130
Tu te prends pour un chat

15:36.700 --> 15:39.480
You think that you're a cat

15:39.480 --> 15:43.170
Comme un jour de la vie

15:39.500 --> 15:43.170
Like a day in life

15:45.630 --> 15:49.210
Une poupée de cire dans soleil

15:45.630 --> 15:49.470
A wax doll in the sun

15:49.470 --> 15:53.840
C'est trop! Qui jouera console?

15:49.470 --> 15:53.840
It's too much! Who'll play console?

15:52.220 --> 15:53.430
Ladies and gentlemen...

15:53.970 --> 15:57.310
...thank you very much for coming today.

15:54.180 --> 15:58.350
Ombrage, orage, oh oh

15:54.180 --> 15:58.350
Shade, storm, oh oh

15:58.100 --> 16:02.100
I'm the general director of the Sharon Apple Galaxy Tour...

16:00.560 --> 16:06.070
Cet amour, l'amour, oh non

16:00.560 --> 16:06.070
This love, love, oh no

16:02.100 --> 16:03.940
Myung Fang Lone.

16:03.940 --> 16:05.270
I'll take any questions you may have now.

16:06.440 --> 16:10.240
The people here on Eden have been eagerly awaiting Sharon's concert.

16:06.610 --> 16:08.820
Quele, quele bouche?

16:06.610 --> 16:08.820
Which, which mouth?

16:08.820 --> 16:10.740
Encore ne qu'elle est

16:08.820 --> 16:10.880
Even though it's only that

16:10.240 --> 16:12.610
Any chance we can get to see her today?

16:10.880 --> 16:14.660
Non, mon petit personnage

16:10.900 --> 16:14.660
No, my little fellow

16:13.110 --> 16:17.740
I'm sorry, but she's resting
right now... Her beauty sleep.

16:17.120 --> 16:19.330
Passé, passé où?

16:17.120 --> 16:19.330
Gone, gone where?

16:19.330 --> 16:21.160
Comme par le passé

16:19.330 --> 16:21.280
Like in the past

16:19.790 --> 16:23.620
They say that Sharon isn't just considered
a computer generated virturoid idol anymore.

16:21.280 --> 16:24.920
Non, mon petit ce n'est rien

16:21.290 --> 16:24.920
No, my little, it's nothing

16:24.080 --> 16:27.340
She's now the number one celebrity everyone wants as a girlfriend.

16:27.340 --> 16:30.130
Sharon's owner, Mr. Reymond, said he wanted to adopt her.

16:31.840 --> 16:35.220
But seriously, some experts say computer generated singing...

16:35.220 --> 16:37.890
...is just a deception, since
computers don't possess emotions.

16:38.470 --> 16:40.060
That's not true at all.

16:40.060 --> 16:42.890
She'd be deeply hurt if she heard that.

16:43.940 --> 16:47.860
Her heart is much more
delicate than a human's.

16:48.270 --> 16:49.730
Oh, did you hear?

16:48.480 --> 16:50.030
Un peu de bleu

16:48.480 --> 16:50.170
A little of blue

16:49.730 --> 16:54.200
That wacko pilot's got the
YF-19 team screwed up big time.

16:50.170 --> 16:53.740
Pour noir de la matière

16:50.190 --> 16:53.740
For the black of the matter

16:55.160 --> 16:57.450
Odds are running 3:1 against them succeeding.

16:57.450 --> 16:59.200
I feel like we've won already.

16:58.950 --> 17:00.490
Un peu de bleu

16:58.950 --> 17:00.540
A little of blue

17:00.080 --> 17:01.830
Don't underestimate him.

17:00.540 --> 17:03.080
Tu te prends pour un chat

17:00.540 --> 17:03.230
You think that you're a cat

17:03.000 --> 17:07.420
Hey, hey... Most of the military guys are betting on our team.

17:03.230 --> 17:06.960
Comme un jour de la vie

17:03.250 --> 17:06.960
Like a day in life

17:07.420 --> 17:08.750
It's in the bag!

17:09.460 --> 17:13.550
So we're looking forward to seeing
everyone at the Atlantis Dome in three days.

17:14.130 --> 17:17.930
And that wraps up the
press conference for today.

17:18.760 --> 17:19.680
Myung...

18:48.440 --> 18:49.900
Will you be done by rehearsal?

18:49.900 --> 18:53.650
It's gonna be real tight. Dammit, I said higher!

18:53.650 --> 18:54.820
Don't let me down.

18:55.860 --> 18:59.070
3-D sound coordinates are off by three points.

18:59.070 --> 19:01.570
Can you shift the BL-unit 1.2 degrees to the right?

19:02.120 --> 19:03.530
BL, to the right!

19:06.580 --> 19:10.500
Dopamine output from block 35-B in the right hemisphere is low.

19:12.170 --> 19:16.460
Do I increase emotion stimulation or change the code to UCL type?

19:16.460 --> 19:20.220
Switch to PSX sampling data and simulate.

19:29.100 --> 19:30.640
Bingo! Bingo!

19:30.640 --> 19:33.730
Give me a bit more stimulation on A-10.

19:33.730 --> 19:36.980
Let's add about three percent of Beta endorphin code.

19:37.690 --> 19:40.450
Myung-san, your taxi's here.

19:41.110 --> 19:44.620
You're scheduled to adjust
Sharon tomorrow afternoon.

19:44.620 --> 19:50.330
Also, I fired two roadies and
replaced them with local crew.

19:50.330 --> 19:52.370
I see. Thank you.

19:52.370 --> 19:53.670
Have a good rest.

20:01.430 --> 20:03.720
That place was packed.

20:04.510 --> 20:07.060
That's where Sharon-chan's concert is gonna be, right?

20:07.060 --> 20:09.390
Everyone's crazy about her.

20:09.390 --> 20:14.650
You know, I even stood in line for that
concert, but all the tickets were sold out!

20:15.900 --> 20:18.980
Everything's changed... Everything...

20:18.980 --> 20:20.780
Yeah.

20:20.780 --> 20:23.530
Development around here's been booming.

20:23.530 --> 20:27.370
About the only things that haven't changed are the forest and the hill.

20:28.240 --> 20:29.330
Star Hill?

20:29.330 --> 20:34.080
Yeah. That place hasn't
changed a bit since I came here.

20:38.420 --> 20:41.800
What's so great about hearing a computer sing?

20:41.800 --> 20:44.180
She isn't an ordinary computer.

20:44.180 --> 20:49.150
Sharon's songs just make me feel... really good.

20:51.520 --> 20:53.730
You really don't know anything.

20:53.730 --> 20:56.900
Couldn't you get news about her in deep space?

20:56.900 --> 21:00.230
Even if I could, I can care less.

21:02.190 --> 21:06.120
Anyway, I'd rather go someplace
where we can get back to nature.

21:08.240 --> 21:12.290
Where real people can hold each other the way nature intended...

21:15.460 --> 21:17.330
You're not into subtlety, are you?

21:18.420 --> 21:20.760
Okay, why don't we go over to Star Hill?

21:23.720 --> 21:25.470
There's nothing there!

21:26.090 --> 21:29.140
What better place for getting back to nature?

22:24.320 --> 22:25.190
Guld...

22:32.580 --> 22:35.750
Why... Why are you here?

22:35.750 --> 22:37.790
I saw you on the news.

22:37.790 --> 22:41.340
I knew if you were on Eden you'd have to come here.

22:47.050 --> 22:48.800
And so you have...

22:51.510 --> 22:55.520
This place hasn't changed. There's nothing here.

22:56.520 --> 22:59.140
A boring place with nothing at all.

22:59.810 --> 23:01.770
How long have you been on Eden?

23:03.110 --> 23:04.730
I just got here yesterday.

23:05.940 --> 23:07.490
It's been seven years...

23:09.910 --> 23:12.320
Do you know about Sharon Apple?

23:13.280 --> 23:17.460
I suppose you could care less about a virturoid idol.

23:17.710 --> 23:22.010
I'm now the producer of the
number one singer in the galaxy.

23:22.250 --> 23:24.590
I've done well for myself, haven't I?

23:24.590 --> 23:25.550
Do you still sing?

23:27.010 --> 23:29.930
I gave it up. A long time ago.

23:30.930 --> 23:32.640
What do you do now?

23:36.600 --> 23:41.690
Testing a prototype fighter out at New Edwards, in the desert.

23:41.690 --> 23:44.860
I see... You're doing well for yourself, too...

23:48.280 --> 23:51.280
I know! Why don't you come to the concert?

23:51.280 --> 23:55.240
I'll abuse my authority as
producer and just let you in.

23:57.160 --> 23:59.910
As a matter of fact, I've just
come from the concert setup.

24:01.250 --> 24:03.460
It'll be the best concert people have ever seen.

24:04.630 --> 24:06.460
Sharon is the best...

24:09.550 --> 24:14.550
Stop it. Just forget what happened back then.

24:19.520 --> 24:21.020
I'll help you forget...

24:37.020 --> 24:39.870
What the heck, there are other people here?

24:43.170 --> 24:44.010
Chief Bowman...

24:57.430 --> 24:59.270
It's been a long time, Isamu.

25:00.810 --> 25:01.730
Who is she?

25:03.060 --> 25:04.940
Have you forgotten me?

25:06.400 --> 25:10.730
Well, well... Little Myung-san, the idol of the school festival.

25:10.730 --> 25:12.620
Didn't know you were Guld's lady now.

25:25.290 --> 25:28.300
Looks like you're the one with no self-control.

25:35.220 --> 25:36.100
Why you...!

25:38.720 --> 25:40.140
Show me what you've got.

25:44.890 --> 25:45.480
Stop it!!!

25:58.490 --> 26:01.420
You never should have come back to Eden.

26:01.790 --> 26:03.450
I won't let you have them...

26:05.040 --> 26:07.460
Not Myung, or the project!

26:10.420 --> 26:12.050
Stop it...

26:13.300 --> 26:14.590
Please, stop it.

26:16.680 --> 26:19.470
It'd be better if you just forgot about me.

26:21.310 --> 26:25.570
I'm not the person you used to know.

26:39.030 --> 26:41.250
Nothing's the same anymore!

26:52.250 --> 26:54.170
I won't let you have them.

26:54.170 --> 26:58.260
Do whatever you want, but the project's mine.

26:58.260 --> 27:00.230
Let a traitor like you get it?!

27:01.300 --> 27:02.300
Never...

27:11.900 --> 27:15.480
Tower to Omega One.
Operation area is all clear.

27:15.480 --> 27:16.910
Atmospheric conditions are excellent.

27:17.150 --> 27:18.240
Roger.

27:18.240 --> 27:20.160
Tower to all chasers.

27:20.160 --> 27:23.530
Activate tracking cameras and transmit video of Omega One.

27:23.530 --> 27:25.290
Chaser Two, roger.

27:25.290 --> 27:26.540
Three, roger.

27:26.540 --> 27:28.910
Chaser One, roger!

27:33.920 --> 27:37.380
Chaser One, just concentrate on
getting a good recording of him.

27:38.420 --> 27:40.470
Why are you trying to screw up this flight?

27:40.470 --> 27:42.770
Don't blame me if you get thrown off the project!

27:42.970 --> 27:45.350
Anger just brings out more freckles, dear.

27:47.850 --> 27:51.850
Tracking camera is standing by.
Sending video now.

27:51.850 --> 27:52.690
Roger.

27:58.900 --> 28:01.040
Omega One to tower.

28:01.240 --> 28:03.120
I've entered the operation area.

28:03.120 --> 28:04.500
Ready when you are.

28:05.280 --> 28:09.290
Control to Omega One. This is Millard.

28:09.290 --> 28:13.130
Bomber Nine will now release
twenty remote control drones...

28:13.130 --> 28:15.040
...which will execute the battle simulation.

28:15.040 --> 28:20.010
This exercise will test air combat and missile avoidance ability.

28:20.590 --> 28:22.590
We expect results better than seventy percent.

28:22.590 --> 28:26.100
Roger. But I guarantee
you one hundred percent.

28:26.100 --> 28:27.400
Very well.

28:40.320 --> 28:43.410
Sixty seconds to target...

28:46.370 --> 28:48.790
I'll show you who the better pilot is.

28:50.790 --> 28:51.960
Stealth...

28:56.590 --> 28:57.880
Not bad.

29:06.430 --> 29:07.980
Let's rock!

29:27.240 --> 29:30.750
Even with boosters I can't keep up with him!

29:35.960 --> 29:38.790
All drones now launching high-maneuver missiles.

29:45.130 --> 29:48.430
The new high-maneuver missiles...

29:49.470 --> 29:51.890
Projected attack area...?

29:57.860 --> 29:58.770
He's accelerating!

29:58.770 --> 29:59.450
The hell...?

29:59.450 --> 30:00.520
He's charging them?!

30:22.380 --> 30:24.470
All missiles avoided...

30:24.470 --> 30:27.390
His relative speed was too fast to trigger their proximity fuses.

30:28.590 --> 30:30.100
Fascinating...

30:32.010 --> 30:34.110
He dodged them all?!

30:34.520 --> 30:36.230
Shit! Where the hell is he?!

30:37.190 --> 30:37.900
What the...?!

30:39.270 --> 30:40.360
Chaser One...

30:40.560 --> 30:42.230
Don't worry.

30:42.230 --> 30:45.110
Those are the dummy missiles the YF-21 has avoided.

30:45.110 --> 30:46.950
You can get hit without danger.

30:46.950 --> 30:49.540
The hell with that! If Guld can do it...

30:49.540 --> 30:51.330
So can I!

31:05.130 --> 31:10.600
Omega One, we will now deploy
twenty drones at 500 behind you.

31:10.600 --> 31:11.930
You can avoid them, can't you?

31:11.930 --> 31:13.180
Allow me to try.

31:13.180 --> 31:17.390
Now, see the true abilities of our YF-21.

31:17.390 --> 31:18.100
T-minus...

31:19.030 --> 31:20.070
three...

31:20.070 --> 31:20.900
two...

31:20.900 --> 31:21.530
one...

31:21.900 --> 31:22.490
Fire!

31:42.840 --> 31:45.500
Shit! Can't control it with the other booster still on!

31:46.260 --> 31:47.390
Just one left...

31:50.550 --> 31:51.390
What?!

31:59.150 --> 32:01.400
Dammit! What the hell's your problem?!

32:17.500 --> 32:18.960
Isamu...!

32:30.590 --> 32:32.130
Trouble with Omega One!

32:32.130 --> 32:34.810
Beta-noise increasing!
Abnormal signal enlarging!

32:35.260 --> 32:38.970
Order an emergency formation! Omega One, bail out at once!

32:38.970 --> 32:40.400
Take emergency formation!

32:40.400 --> 32:43.560
No... I can recover by myself...

32:47.610 --> 32:49.900
Omega One! Bail out!

32:49.900 --> 32:51.530
I can get her back!

32:54.250 --> 32:57.410
Man... This new fighter really is something.

32:57.410 --> 32:59.210
Looks great even going down in flames!

33:01.540 --> 33:05.340
Altitude 800... 750... 700...

33:05.340 --> 33:06.840
650...

33:06.840 --> 33:08.170
600...

33:08.170 --> 33:09.880
550...

33:09.880 --> 33:10.890
500... No change yet!

33:11.590 --> 33:14.180
450... 400...

33:14.180 --> 33:15.640
This doesn't look good!

33:15.640 --> 33:17.480
350... 300...

33:17.890 --> 33:20.440
250... 200...

33:20.440 --> 33:25.650
Chaser One! Rescue him or your flight clearance is revoked!

33:26.610 --> 33:29.020
Do you copy that, Chaser One?

33:31.240 --> 33:33.900
Can't disobey a direct order, can I?

33:43.500 --> 33:44.710
Get away!

34:13.030 --> 34:14.860
How dare you...!

34:16.820 --> 34:23.330
If the YF-21 were to generate a
downward force right now, he'd...

34:27.090 --> 34:27.800
Wha...?!

35:14.300 --> 35:15.300
You son of a bitch!

35:15.710 --> 35:17.630
What the hell did you do that for?!

35:18.380 --> 35:21.260
Oh? So you're still alive.

35:21.260 --> 35:22.890
You must have the devil's own luck.

35:25.220 --> 35:26.390
You...

35:27.480 --> 35:28.480
You did it on purpose?!

35:39.320 --> 35:41.820
I'm sorry. It was an accident.

